th Spitz surprisingly last at that point. He was challenged on the third lap by Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/47451"} "Martyn Woodroffe"] ", but Robie never lost the lead and held on in the final lap to win gold by 0.3 seconds, Woodroffe placing second. " [:a {:href "/athletes/51334"} "John Ferris"] " of the United States was third for most of the race and won the bronze medal, with Spitz a badly beaten eighth and last in the final. He would do a bit better in 1972, winning gold in this race, and fulfilling his prediction there to win seven gold medals."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "15364"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51534"} "Carl Robie"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "2:11.1 (2 h5)"] [:td {} "2:08.7 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "16688"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47451"} "Martyn Woodroffe"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "2:11.6 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "2:09.0 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "15346"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51334"} "John Ferris"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "2:10.6 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "2:09.3 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]]